{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# DC segmenting Markdown to wiki renderer\n\n## Problem and boundaries\nJira Data Center stores wiki markup while rebar authors Markdown. DC sends Markdown literally. Whole-body pandoc 3.6.1 was measured to escape prose/code arrows, erode table delimiters, and delete the <!-- rebar:reconciler-echo --> marker.\n\nThis story adds an unwired pure renderer. WikiTextCodec.fit_outbound retains 32,767-character truncation; normalize_outbound/to_wire remain string identity; decode_inbound retains string identity and None-to-empty. OutboundFieldMapper, CREATE, normalize_rich_text, and live send paths stay unchanged. Story 3388 owns cutover, echo suppression, and convergence. Story 5c0e owns timeout/process and GPL/SBOM hardening before cutover. Cloud uses ADF and its separate child.\n\nADR 0083 governs imports. Add ADR 0095 plus docs/adr/.numbers/0095 for the selective-rendering decision, invariants, dependency-pin rationale, comparison with pure-Python converters, and deferred boundaries.\n\n## Corpus\nThe prior ephemeral export is unavailable, so its 179/70 and 68/78 claims are not acceptance evidence. Commit a deterministic scrubbed sample generated by scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py: 29 code-arrow, 29 table, and 120 prose bodies, 178 total. The fixed-seed generator scrubs before writing, includes every available protected-phenomenon body plus prose, and keeps shards below 500 KB.\n\nRecords declare source text, protected excerpts, and eligible safe units; they are not generated from renderer output. Add tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus to EXCLUDED_PREFIXES in scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py. Tests reject emails, tenant hostnames, and URLs.\n\nRendered-body ratio = bodies with at least one safe unit successfully changed by real pandoc / 178. Rendered-character ratio = sum of source characters in successfully changed eligible safe units / sum of source characters in all eligible safe units across all 178 bodies. Independently measured values are 0.927 and 0.984; tests require >=0.90 and >=0.95. Identity fallback fails because eligible safe-unit outputs must differ.\n\n## Renderer contract\nAdd adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py with render_markdown_to_wiki(markdown: str) -> str.\n\nUse a two-phase left-to-right lexer:\n1. Lock complete existing {noformat} spans and backtick/tilde fenced blocks, including internal blank lines.\n2. Split only intervening text into blank-line blocks and list items; preserve separators/order.\n\nClassify in order:\n1. Locked blocks and already-wiki units beginning h1.-h6., {code}, {noformat}, or {{ pass exactly.\n2. ASCII table = >=2 pipe-bearing lines with a delimiter row of pipes/colons/hyphens/whitespace. Wrap exact bytes once in {noformat}.\n3. HTML-dangerous = HTML comment or tag matching <[/!]?[A-Za-z][^>]*>; pass exactly.\n4. Regex-dangerous = outside-code text containing group opener (?; backslash class \\b/\\d/\\s/\\w; or bracket class followed by a quantifier; pass exactly.\n5. Remaining headings, quotes, list items, and prose render with pypandoc input commonmark, output jira, --wrap=none.\n\nCode fragments are fenced blocks, four-space-indented blocks, and inline spans delimited by matching backtick runs. Extract before arrow work. Protected blocks never reach substitution. In safe units use one regex pass ordered <!--, -->, <->, ->, <-, =>. Map arrows to ↔, →, ←, ⇒; HTML delimiters map to themselves. Sequential replacement is forbidden. Inline code copies exactly.\n\nAfter conversion, every extracted code fragment must appear byte-identically and in order; otherwise return that source unit. Strip pandoc's content-free {anchor:} emitted after headings. Already-wiki input stays exact, making repeated rendering deterministic.\n\nMissing pypandoc returns the whole body and logs a structured warning without content. Conversion exception or preservation rejection returns that unit and logs a structured debug fallback class without content. Module state is immutable.\n\n## Dependency and CI\nAdd wiki = [\"pypandoc-binary==1.15\"] and include wiki in dev. Register wiki in rebar._optional.EXTRAS with pypandoc probe; regenerate uv.lock. In .github/workflows/_optionality.yml add standalone wiki:wiki, remove the stale eval:eval spec, and change the joint lane from union:agents,eval,tracing to union:agents,tracing,wiki. Existing optionality parity and removed-eval tests remain green.\n\nA non-skipping test requires pypandoc.get_pandoc_version() == \"3.6.1\", asserts \"jira\" is present in pypandoc.get_pandoc_formats()[1], and performs real commonmark-to-jira conversion, so a version, writer, or platform mismatch fails CI.\n\nChanged paths are src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py; scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py; tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/; tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py; tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_corpus.py; pyproject.toml; uv.lock; src/rebar/_optional.py; .github/workflows/_optionality.yml; scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py; docs/adr/0095-dc-segmenting-wiki-renderer.md; and docs/adr/.numbers/0095.\n\n## Verification\nAuthor all tests RED-first and collect nodes without skip/xfail. Run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`, `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`, and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test`.\n\nNo contention test applies: stateless transform/local process boundary; no store composition, retry/backoff, or cached store state.\n\n## Surface parity\nCLI, MCP/API, public facade: out of scope; capability is internal. Automated callers and dual-direction: story 3388. Cloud: ADF child.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Safe units render through real pandoc in order; test_dc_segmenting_passthrough.\n- [ ] Tables preserve exact bytes; test_dc_segmenting_passthrough.\n- [ ] HTML/regex-dangerous units preserve exact bytes; test_dc_segmenting_passthrough.\n- [ ] Specified single-pass arrows convert prose; test_arrow_substitution_cases.\n- [ ] Code arrows and --> remain exact; test_dc_arrow_substitution_spares_code.\n- [ ] All 29 code-arrow fixtures retain protected excerpts; test_dc_corpus_no_code_arrow_is_ever_rewritten.\n- [ ] All 29 table fixtures keep exact tables inside one noformat wrapper over five passes; test_dc_table_noformat_stable and test_dc_corpus_tables_survive_verbatim.\n- [ ] HTML comments survive exactly; test_dc_corpus_html_comments_survive.\n- [ ] Existing wiki/noformat bodies stay exact over five passes; test_dc_already_wiki_body_passes_through and test_dc_corpus_render_is_deterministic_across_passes.\n- [ ] Missing pandoc returns exact body; test_dc_pandoc_absent_identity.\n- [ ] Missing-pandoc warning contains no body; test_dc_pandoc_absent_identity.\n- [ ] Conversion/preservation failure returns exact unit; test_dc_pandoc_failure_degrades_that_unit.\n- [ ] Failure log names only fallback class; test_dc_pandoc_failure_degrades_that_unit.\n- [ ] wiki locks pypandoc-binary 1.15, installs standalone, and jointly resolves without removed eval; optionality lane.\n- [ ] Real binary reports pandoc 3.6.1 and exposes jira writer; test_dc_real_pandoc_version.\n- [ ] Rendered-body ratio >=0.90; test_dc_corpus_coverage.\n- [ ] Rendered-character ratio >=0.95 over eligible safe-unit source characters; test_dc_corpus_coverage.\n- [ ] Cardinality = 29+29+120=178; test_corpus_cardinality_is_pinned.\n- [ ] Fixtures contain no email, tenant hostname, or URL; test_corpus_carries_no_unscrubbed_secrets.\n- [ ] ADR 0095 and marker exist; check_adr_numbers.py passes, and the ADR contains Decision, Invariants, Dependency Pin, Alternatives, and Deferred Boundaries headings verified by test_wiki_render.py.\n- [ ] Existing WikiTextCodec tests stay unmodified and green under make test."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786571468500904001,"uuid":"2ddcb48e-7c4e-418a-926a-4862c7af529b"}